\text{and}\\,\\,Y\\le 4)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,Y\\le 4) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(2,2),(2,4)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(2,2))+P((X,Y)=(2,4)) \\\\  & =f(2,2)+f(2,4) \\\\  & =0.05+0.15 \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247025 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162073 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e20c64-85be-5cb5-acde-17ffd8b6aff5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "039b80b2-527f-56cc-a9bc-ff3bc90ac111" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244338} {:answer/id #uuid "27f7a13e-be49-5079-b844-a4c3415b2fd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244665} {:answer/id #uuid "adbb15ed-5e20-5e15-ac70-ff60a0a5d46d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245865} {:answer/id #uuid "b6826898-2df3-5edc-9c17-76d4e6512dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245945} {:answer/id #uuid "b6eb299c-829c-5764-a80a-06bf21a8c82e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6826898-2df3-5edc-9c17-76d4e6512dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245945} :answer-field/id #uuid "89831f9f-6346-59a1-a3f3-bf51f497aaa9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246786}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "89e9e61a-c7f2-587b-936c-fdec6e3defa1" :question/math-academy-id "q-109687" :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.2$ | $0.12$ | $0.23$ |\n\nCalculate $P(X+Y=1)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X+Y=1) & =P(X=0,Y=1)+P(X=1,Y=0) \\\\  & =f(0,1)+f(1,0) \\\\  & =0.25+0.2 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
